# Stackra file contract:
# Purpose: what git never tracks in the public site: everything stackra gen writes into .stackra/
#          and the root shims of the generated tool configs, and the build, Worker, test and
#          Lighthouse output. The committed contract, stackra.manifest.json, sits at the member
#          root, outside .stackra/.
# Boundary: ignore rules only; the subset of the root .gitignore this member relies on, repeated so
#           the folder keeps its rules when copied out of the workspace.
# Runtime: node
# Governing contract: Stackra ADR 0294 decision 10 (generated output is never authored), ADR 0295
#                     decision 5 (generated tool configs and their root shims)

# everything gen writes: the runtime entries, the gen modules, the React Router files, the tool
# configs and the Worker config
.stackra/*
# the root shims of the generated configs, for tools that read only the member root (Vite, Vitest,
# Playwright, React Router, Wrangler and Lighthouse CI)
/vite.config.ts
/vitest.config.ts
/playwright.config.ts
/react-router.config.ts
/wrangler.jsonc
/lighthouserc.yaml
# template only: the generated samples are committed so they can be read beside their source; a
# real project drops this line once `stackra gen` runs in it (the same change in every member and
# the root)
!.stackra/**
# React Router's client and server build (the Worker serves build/client as static assets)
build/
# wrangler's local state from `stackra start` (KV, cache, Durable Object storage of dev runs)
.wrangler/
# React Router's generated route types (`+types/*`), rebuilt on every dev and build run
.react-router/
# Playwright's traces, screenshots and videos of failed journeys
test-results/
# Playwright's HTML report
playwright-report/
# Lighthouse CI's local reports
.lighthouseci/
